From c027a92857fab810f00a3d801ddda35f8e13c1da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dre Gilley <dre@dregilley.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:20:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] WIP: soundd/micd: 90 s audio retry, block engagement
 until soundd's stream is open

On this comma 4 the audio device becomes openable 25-39 s after manager start;
soundd/micd gave up after 10 x 3 s and stayed dead while onroad
(processNotRunning for the whole drive, 5 of 21 cold-boot starts).

- soundd/micd: retry 30 x 3 s
- soundd_ready.py: /dev/shm marker with soundd's PID, written atomically once
  the output stream is open; cleared when soundd starts
- selfdrived: raise processNotRunning until the marker matches the running
  soundd (10 Hz check, latched, bypassed in REPLAY/SIMULATION); not
  selfdriveInitializing, which card.py uses to gate CAN output
- events: "Process Not Running: soundd (audio starting)" when no process is down

Tests: 33 new; 80/80 with the existing soundd/selfdrived/MADS tests (x86 shim).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
